message: "If you use this software, please cite the article and this software."
title: "EEG evaluation audit: evaluation schemes, dependence-preserving permutation tests and simulations for window-based EEG classification"
abstract: "Analysis code accompanying Cho and Kim, 'Random data splitting and window-level significance tests overstate evidence from EEG classification: dependence-preserving permutation tests, design comparisons and simulations'. Implements random-window, within-recording time and cross-subject evaluation; binomial, window-level and dependence-preserving permutation tests; label-free diagnostics (time-block pseudo-labels, participant identification); a replication on a public dataset with block and interleaved designs; and ground-truth and data-calibrated simulations, including type I error and power of evaluation-scheme x test combinations."
version: "1.3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - EEG
  - brain-computer interface
  - data leakage
  - cross-validation
  - permutation test
  - exchangeability
